2026-06-30 13:01:56,883 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: As a Security & Compliance Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I can confirm that our company has experience with regulatory frameworks such as GDPR and RGS v2. We have a Data Protection Officer appointed, and their contact information is dpo@nexus-engineering.it. Our standard data residency policy is to store data within the EU only, and we have a cross-border transfer policy that prohibits transfers outside the EU unless there's an explicit legal basis.

To ensure GDPR compliance, our solution will implement anonymization tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models. We also have a capability for Data Protection Impact Assessment with an average duration of 3 weeks. Our access control standards include multi-factor authentication enforced through TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), and we use Role-Based Access Control design experience and Privileged Access Management solutions like CyberArk Conjur and HashiCorp Vault.

For data protection, our AI security controls include prompt injection protection, output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, confidence threshold escalation, model isolation through inference API only, and model update security review. We also have a logging and auditing system that logs all queries, with immutable logs using append-only with SHA-256 hash chaining, and we retain audit logs for 7 years.

To prevent unauthorized access or transfer of data outside the EU, our network security architecture follows zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth patterns. We have Intrusion Detection and Prevention Systems deployed and conduct annual penetration testing plus post-major release testing with partners like Synacktiv and HN Security.

Our solution will be designed to ensure explicability and transparency, with measures in place to provide explicit validation of agent decisions and guarantee response times compatible with daily use by agents. We will also ensure that our solution is hosted exclusively within the European Union, using infrastructure that guarantees sovereignty of data, such as SecNumCloud-type infrastructure or equivalent.

We believe our company's existing security and compliance posture can meet the requirements specified in the tender, and we are committed to protecting sensitive data and preventing unauthorized access or transfer outside the EU.
